course: dictionary
lesson: 206
title: Alcohol: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Alcohol is a word with more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. «Many grown-ups drink things that change how they feel» is about drinks. In «rubbing alcohol», it means a liquid used for cleaning and killing germs. The clues show you which meaning to choose.
explain: «Cigarettes, vapes and alcohol harm a growing body.» This sentence tells you that alcohol can hurt you, especially while your body is still growing. «When you cook with alcohol, some of it always stays in the food» shows that alcohol is used in cooking too, but not all of it disappears.
explain: Alcohol is a drug. It slows down the brain and body, which is why it is against the law for children to buy it and why adults must never drink and drive. «Substance misuse» is the official British phrase for harmful use of drugs or alcohol.
explain: Never drink from an unknown bottle or glass, and never drink hand sanitiser or cleaning alcohol. If someone is very drunk and unwell, tell an adult straight away. Staying safe is the most important thing to remember from this lesson.
fact: Alcohol has three meanings: a drink that can make you drunk, a drink that contains it, and a cleaning liquid that kills germs.
fact: Alcohol is uncountable, so you say some alcohol, not two alcohols.
fact: Alcohol is a drug that slows the brain and body, and it is especially harmful to children's growing brains.
fact: It is against the law for children to buy alcohol.
fact: Hand sanitiser and rubbing alcohol are poisonous to drink, and alcohol evaporates quickly and burns.
exercise: «Cigarettes, vapes and alcohol harm a growing body.» What does this sentence tell you about alcohol? | *It can harm a growing body | It is good for your teeth | It is safe to share with friends | It helps children grow taller
exercise: A friend finds hand sanitiser and says, «I'll drink some, it's alcohol.» What should you do? | Drink a little, because it is safe | Pour it into a glass for a friend | *Tell an adult and do not drink it | Mix it with juice first
exercise: «When you cook with alcohol, some of it always stays in the food.» What does this tell you? | Cooking always removes every drop | Food with alcohol is always sweet | *Cooking does not remove all the alcohol | Alcohol cannot be used in cooking
test: «"In recovery" means recovering from an addiction, such as to alcohol or drugs, and staying off it.» What does staying off it mean? | Forgetting its name | Drinking it slowly | *Keeping away from it | Going out to buy it
test: Why is it against the law for children to buy alcohol? | *Because it slows the brain and body and harms a growing child | Because it tastes bad | Because it is sold only in summer | Because it is too expensive for shops
exam: Which meaning of alcohol fits «rubbing alcohol»? | A small animal that lives in water | A sweet fizzy drink for children | *A liquid used for cleaning and killing germs | A kind of food for growing bodies
